      "en": "PROLOGUE."
    },
    {
      "la": "CAP. I. Quod Maria in consensu conjugali virginitatis propositam non mutavit.",
      "column": "857a",
      "chunk": 1,
      "en": "CHAP. I. That Mary did not change the purpose of virginity in her conjugal consent."
    },
    {
      "la": "CAP. II. Quod sacrosancta et perpetua virgo Maria non de viro, sed de Spiritu sancto concepit, quem et peperit Altissimi Patris unigenitum, Christum Deum et hominem.",
      "column": "870c",
      "chunk": 5,
      "en": "CHAP. II. That the most holy and perpetual virgin Mary conceived not of a man, but of the Holy Spirit, whom she also bore, the only-begotten of the Most High Father, Christ, God and man."
    },
    {
      "la": "CAP. III. Quod sine doloris et sine virginitatis detrimento Maria Christum peperit.",
      "column": "872c",
      "chunk": 5,
      "en": "CHAP. III. That Mary bore Christ without detriment of pain and without detriment of virginity."
    },
    {
      "la": "CAP. IV. Quaestio, utrum probabile sit, matrimonium sine consensu coitus contrahi posse.",
      "column": "873b",
      "chunk": 6,
      "en": "CHAP. IV. A question: whether it is probable that matrimony can be contracted without consent to intercourse."
    }
  ],
  "headnotes": [
    {
      "la": "…rgunculam nostram singulariter castam, excellenter speciosam, unice mundam. Sed ego novi oculum tuum, quia lippus est, et quanto diligentius intenditur, tanto iniquius contemplatur. Lex, inquit, dixit",
      "en": "…irgin, singularly chaste, excellently beautiful, uniquely clean. But I know your eye, that it is bleary, and the more diligently it is strained, the more wrongly it beholds. The Law, he says, has said",
